+# GitLab pilot adapter
+
+This fork supports Feishu-origin tickets against one GitLab project. Enable `dsh-superagent-gitlab` and disable `dsh-superagent-github` in the DSH profile. Engine, ticket lifecycle, executor sessions, worktree preparation and Feishu outbox remain shared with the original implementation.
+
+## Source configuration
+
+Save `source:gitlab` with `enabled: true` and a config containing `host`, `repository` (including nested groups), `cli` (absolute glab wrapper path) and `pollSeconds` (default 30).
+
+Setup checks a non-administrator account, Developer-or-higher access, exact project path and non-archived state. Source API requests use the returned numeric project ID and explicitly configured host. Internal URLs advertised by reverse-proxied GitLab are replaced by the configured HTTPS origin, including MR links and clone URLs.
+
+`Deployment.github` remains a legacy execution-identity field. Optional `Deployment.gitlab` selects the platform. GitHub API methods and the worker gh shim reject calls in GitLab mode. A glab shim and host-specific Git credential helper use the bot account.
+
+## Delivery and follow-up
+
+A worker branch must end with `DSH_SUPERAGENT_NAME`. Workers report `mr_number` (project-local MR IID), not `pr_number`. Before binding, the host verifies author, source/target project, branch and competing active ticket ownership. Polling recovers an unreported open bot-authored MR that uniquely matches a ticket branch.
+
+The source polls bound MR notes, head pipeline status and merged/closed state. Stable Trigger IDs deduplicate repeated reads. A ready report with an open MR leaves the ticket awaiting review. Closure uses the Engine's existing completion rules and emits a terminal chat notice. MR replies include a marker to suppress sequential retry duplicates; this is not distributed exactly-once delivery.
+
+## Pilot boundaries
+
+- New work starts in Feishu; repository-wide issue/MR intake is not implemented.
+- Workers may create GitLab issues when authorized, but mandatory issue registration is not implemented.
+- Bound MR discussions, top-level note replies and pipeline events are supported. Inline discussion resolution and automated review approvals are not implemented.
+- GitLab execution instructions prohibit automatic merging and default-branch pushes. Repository protection should independently enforce the team's rules.
+- The service is single-process and retains the existing state-directory lock.
+- The pilot allows all members of its configured Feishu group to originate work by mentioning the bot. Private chats and other groups remain off.
+- Concurrency is two Workers on the current approximately 2 GB server, as requested by the operator; further requests queue. Concurrent build memory has not yet been measured.
+
+## Verification
+
+`tests/gitlab.spec.ts` covers nested namespaces, permissions, reverse-proxy URL normalization, project-scoped API calls, MR ownership and terminal notices. Existing core, deployment, environment, tools and source tests still apply.
+
+After installation health checks, first send a read-only README request in Feishu. A separately requested code change is needed to verify the complete worktree, validation, push, MR review and closure flow. Healthy installation does not prove that full workflow has already run.
